      "id": "1ed15bf153feca7f81461bd8d91693cb24f9f2cb",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1679: the part fits the wire\n\nAn OTA-1677 regression, found reviewing the owner's 01:50 push \u2014 the first\nfull logs sent under 1677.\n\nMEASURED\nEvery one of the 56 full parts in the two bundles came back as 33\u201337 blocks\nwhose JSON ran 16,413\u201316,424 characters, the last block cut mid-string\n(undecodable) and every block after it gone. 11,891 of 15,000 characters\nsurvived per part: a 21% hole in every log, where 1520's problem had been one\n400-character block in 29% of events. The assembled logs read 332,519 of the\n399,911 characters the device said it sent.\n\nWHY\nOTA-1677 base64-encoded every block so the scrubber is handed no text. It was\nmeasured against the scrubber and it won. It was never measured against\nSentry's TRIM of the `extra` value: a 15,000-character raw part encodes to\n~20,000 characters of array, and Sentry cuts the value at a fixed budget. The\npre-1677 part (15,000 raw, ~15.1K of JSON) had sat just under that budget,\nwhich is why the trim had never shown itself in a year of parts.\n\nFIX\nParts are packed by ENCODED cost, not cut by raw length. `packLogIntoParts`\nencodes every block first and closes a part when the next block would push\nits JSON past INLINE_PART_BUDGET_CHARS (14,000 \u2014 a fifth under the measured\ntrim) or its raw text past INLINE_CHUNK_CHARS (now 10,000, the ceiling rather\nthan the cut). Nothing the log contains can push a part past the budget: a\nrun of three-byte glyphs encodes to four times its character count and the\npacker counts what the wire will carry. `chunkChars` stays the raw receipt,\nthe relay is unchanged, and a part count is whatever the packing produced.\n\nPROVEN: the suite packs a real 400 KB delivered log from the inbox and a\n60,000-glyph worst case, and checks every part under budget, every raw part\nunder the ceiling, every block whole, and the join exact.\n\n- app/diagnostics/sentryTransport.ts \u2014 INLINE_PART_BUDGET_CHARS,\n  packLogIntoParts, INLINE_CHUNK_CHARS 15,000 \u2192 10,000; sendGameLogInline\n  ships the packed parts.\n- __tests__/ota1679ThePartFitsTheWire.test.ts \u2014 7 tests.\n- __tests__/ota1518, ota1520, ota1677 \u2014 the sender-shape pins repointed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
